<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper C · Learner paper · 繁體</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/c/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper C</p><h1>Learner paper · 繁體</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 C</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">圖書角: classroom book corner</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first join an activity in the new class?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 去年九月開學前的最後一週</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年九月開學後的第二週</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年九月開學後的第一天</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">軟件: software</p><p class="gloss">資格: qualification</p><p class="gloss">標誌: sign</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What had the man originally thought he needed before helping?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先把所有同學的住址記住</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先請別人替他畫上學路線</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先學會很難的軟件</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why does he prepare a route drawing for the next discussion?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 同學已經決定以後不再使用地圖軟件</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他發現下午的小門已經改成全天開放</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 同學需要他熟悉的路線信息，不只是軟件操作</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">講解: explanation</p><p class="gloss">對應: corresponding</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What does the woman explicitly want to do first?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 馬上完整看完講解視頻再讀文章</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 獨立讀幾分鐘，找出自己不懂的地方</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先把所有問題交給同伴代寫</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What best explains the man’s final arrangement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 讓視頻代替原文，以後不必再讀句子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求所有人先提出完全相同的問題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 保留獨立閱讀，也讓視頻回應實際遇到的問題</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">短片: short video</p><p class="gloss">參觀: visit/tour</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do first for the holiday project?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 選三個地方寫介紹，並排出參觀順序</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先買新相機，再決定介紹哪些地方</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把拍攝全部完成以後才準備介紹詞</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">耳機: headphones</p><p class="gloss">名額: available place</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What does Course A require?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 有電腦和耳機，並連續四周按時參加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只帶紙筆，任選一個週六參加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只在第一週借到電腦就能完成全部課程</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits the man’s circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲本週六沒空，就放棄所有以後場次</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 詢問乙下週的內容和名額，確認後單次報名</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只借一週電腦，直接承諾上完甲四周</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">片段: short extract</p><p class="gloss">順序: sequence</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for preparing the listening extract?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 小許</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 負責記錄問題的女生</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 負責發出安排的男生</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What sequence have they agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一邊播放一邊討論，直到講完每道題</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先獨立聽，再對答案，集中討論兩個問題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先等老師答覆所有問題，再開始聽音頻</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">校園廣播: school radio broadcast</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of this broadcast?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分享新同學選擇學習地點的經歷和理由</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 宣佈全校每個學生必須使用的固定座位</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只按座位數量給所有教室排名</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">播音員: radio announcer</p><p class="gloss">停頓: pause</p><p class="gloss">交稿: submit a script/recording</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Jilan’s approach change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從急着模仿聲音，變爲用自己的聲音清楚表達內容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 從自己寫稿，變爲請朋友代錄全部節目</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 從檢查內容，變爲只追求說話速度</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude is best supported by the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 可以保留個人表達方式，同時認真檢查是否說清楚</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要用自己的聲音，就完全不必修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有聽起來和播音員完全一樣才值得發表</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">提示牌: information sign</p><p class="gloss">小苗: young seedlings</p><p class="gloss">可重複使用: reusable</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. Which rule must participants follow during the check?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 爲了看清提示牌，可以穿過所有草地</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每個人必須自帶滿電手機和相機</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 走小路，不進入新種小苗的區域</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan lets the man contribute with his available resources?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 放棄記錄，只能等買新手機後再參加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 穿過小苗儘快拍照，以免手機電量用完</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 沿小路用記錄板記問題，照片需要時請老師拍</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">餐具: cutlery</p><p class="gloss">歸還: return a borrowed item</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. When can students now collect the cutlery?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週三午休</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週四上課前</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週四放學後</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">戲劇社: drama club</p><p class="gloss">收穫: something learned/gained</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What does Xiaoxia now do before leaving detailed discussion until the weekend?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天晚上把所有羣消息都重新讀完</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 用十分鐘記一個收穫和一個問題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先退出戲劇社，不再和同伴交流</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which combination explains why she wants to continue this arrangement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 她從此不看任何通知，也不準備上學用品</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 兩週記錄已經證明每個人都必須照此生活</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先記下問題，週末再聊，減少每晚等消息且仍保留交流</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">重點: main point</p><p class="gloss">塞進去: cram into</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which adjustment fits the woman’s short practice periods?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天增加到一小時，把所有細節都背下來</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 選一個重點，分次練開頭和一個例子</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等能一次講完全部內容纔開始任何練習</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What changed view is supported by the man’s memory?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 介紹不必一次說完所有事，有意義的追問也值得重視</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要有人提問，準備內容就沒有必要</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 任何超時的介紹都會得到完全一樣的好結果</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年三月，我轉到現在的班級。第二次班會時，老師讓大家給新同學寫一張小卡片，介紹一個自己喜歡的校園地點。我收到的第一張上寫着“午休來窗邊的長桌，可以一起畫畫”。那天我沒有馬上去，只先回了一句謝謝。週五我帶着紙筆去試了試，後來常在那裏見到寫卡片的人。</p></div><p class="gloss">轉到: transfer to</p><p class="gloss">班會: class meeting</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did classmates write the cards for new students?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 去年三月轉班前的最後一次活動</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年三月轉班後的第二次班會</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年三月第一次參加繪畫比賽時</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">剛轉班時，小齊被邀請參加午休的桌面遊戲。她以前只在家和弟弟玩，擔心規則不一樣，自己輸了以後大家就不想再邀請她。第一輪她一直不敢問，走錯了一步。她想收好東西離開，旁邊的小文卻把說明書轉過來，請大家一起看那一條規則。<br>看完以後，小齊發現另外兩個同學也記錯了。他們重新試了一輪，還請她說說在家玩的不同方法。第二天她沒有提前練到每一步都不會錯，而是帶了一張自己寫的問題紙。有人建議換一種遊戲時，她先問需要幾個人、能玩多久，再決定參加。她後來記住的，不是第一輪輸了多少，而是大家願意把規則說明白的樣子。</p></div><p class="gloss">桌面遊戲: tabletop game</p><p class="gloss">規則: rules</p><p class="gloss">說明書: instruction booklet</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What had Xiaoqi feared before the first round?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 其他同學會要求她先教弟弟玩</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有人都會拒絕查看說明書</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 輸了以後大家不再邀請她</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why does she return with questions rather than trying to eliminate every possible mistake?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲她已經確定所有遊戲規則都完全相同</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 共同查規則的經歷表明，不懂時可以一起問清楚</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因爲小文替她承諾以後每次都一定贏</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小組通知：週四下午六點前，每人交一份中文使用說明，只要文字，不用交視頻。小岑負責把大家的內容放在同一頁上，週五午休請新成員試讀，看看步驟是否清楚。——小許<br>小川回覆：學校借我的電腦今晚要歸還，到週五才能再用。我已在紙上寫好四個步驟，週四午休能借同伴的手機拍給你。每步的序號都在，第二步我加了一個例子。我想請你先看看照片裏的字是否清楚；如果有地方太小，我午休還能重新拍。我擔心你以爲必須有視頻，才一直想等電腦借回來。現在知道通知只要文字，就能按時準備了。</p></div><p class="gloss">序號: step number</p><p class="gloss">試讀: try reading</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What does each member have to submit by Thursday at 6 p.m.?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一份中文文字使用說明，不必有視頻</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已經錄好的完整中文演示視頻</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 新成員週五試讀後的全部反饋</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. How can Xiaocen keep Xiaochuan’s part on schedule for the Friday trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 等他週五借回電腦、補完視頻後纔開始整理</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週四檢查照片是否清楚，再整理其中的文字</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只收電子打印稿，因此直接刪掉他的部分</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">暑假我想學設計活動海報。這周先找幾份校園公告，比較標題、時間和地點放在哪裏，再用紙筆給熟悉的社團畫一張草稿。週末請同學只看草稿，找出報名時間。如果不好找，就先調整位置，不急着學複雜的軟件。我希望開始學工具以前，先知道自己要讓讀者看清什麼。</p></div><p class="gloss">海報: poster</p><p class="gloss">標題: heading/title</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is the writer’s immediate preparation for poster design?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 比較公告的信息位置，畫草稿並請同學試讀</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先學會複雜軟件，再第一次查看校園公告</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 印好所有正式海報後，才確認報名時間</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">假期項目公告：甲是故事剪輯，週二和週四上午各上一次課，報名時須已有一份故事腳本；費用四十元。乙是圖文導覽，週五下午上一次課，須帶三張自己拍的地點照片和紙筆；免費。兩項都可借用現場電腦，報名截止時間同爲下週一中午。<br>小舟給同伴的回覆：我下週二、週四上午要陪家人辦事，週五下午有空。我最想把校園裏容易走錯的地方介紹清楚，上週已經拍了幾張路口照片，還沒有寫故事腳本。我準備這個週末選出三張，想好每張要說明什麼，週一登記前再確認乙是否有位置。電腦可以現場借，不必因爲我家沒有電腦就放棄。</p></div><p class="gloss">腳本: script</p><p class="gloss">圖文導覽: picture-and-text guide</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which difference between the projects is correctly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲提供現場電腦，乙完全不許借電腦</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要已有故事腳本，乙要自攝地點照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲免費，乙必須交四十元材料費</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which next step fits Xiaozhou’s interest, resources and schedule?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先爲甲寫腳本，忽略週二和週四的時間衝突</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 選三張路口照片並確認乙名額，週一截止前登記</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 必須先買一臺電腦，纔有資格問乙的名額</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校園廣播通知：每組週五上午十點前交一段不超過一分鐘的介紹錄音，並附上完全對應的文字稿。不要只交背景音樂。小組可自己分工，不要求每個人都錄音。老師會按文字稿覈對聽不清的地方。<br>小嵐：我想寫文字稿，坐車時也能在本子上改。小陸：我家晚上比較安靜，我來錄音，不過希望先有確定的內容，不想一邊錄一邊等修改。小嵐：週三我先發草稿，大家週四午休覈對，晚上你錄。週五九點我們一起聽一次，九點半把錄音和最後文字稿一起交。小陸：好，臨時改了詞也要在文字稿上改，不能留下兩個不同版本。</p></div><p class="gloss">對應: correspond exactly</p><p class="gloss">版本: version</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. Why does Xiaolan offer to write the script?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 坐車時也可以在本子上修改</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 她家晚上比所有人家裏都安靜</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 通知規定每個人必須各錄一段</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Which plan meets both the notice and the group’s agreement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週五九點半隻交音樂，文字稿下週再補</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週四錄好舊稿，週五改文字但不檢查是否對應</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週四核稿後錄音，週五九點半交對應的兩份材料</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校園節目本週介紹原創短故事《路過的窗》。主人公每天急着走同一條路，後來爲新同學帶路，才第一次停下來看窗邊的介紹牌。節目不把他變成無所不知的嚮導，而是選取前後兩次經過同一地點的片段，請聽衆比較他注意了什麼。想討論日常細節的同學，可以帶一個問題來聽。</p></div><p class="gloss">嚮導: guide</p><p class="gloss">無所不知: know everything</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What does the programme invite listeners to compare?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 人物前後經過同一地點時注意到的內容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有校園嚮導背誦地名的速度</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 兩所不同學校裏窗戶的數量</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原創故事《沒送到的卡片》裏，新來的安禾看到同學們週末活動的照片，卻沒有收到邀請。她以爲大家不想帶她一起，第二天把原來準備的小禮物收進了抽屜。午休時，小林來問她爲什麼沒到，還拿出一張寫着舊教室號碼的邀請卡，才知道他一直把卡放在她以前班級的桌上。<br>安禾先說自己昨天有些難過，又問下一次活動怎樣確認時間地點。她沒有假裝什麼也沒發生，也沒有繼續不問就認定別人不歡迎她。後來小林把新卡遞到她手裏，她讀了一遍時間，再請他指給自己看集合處。禮物仍在抽屜裏，她想等下次真正見面時再帶過去。</p></div><p class="gloss">邀請卡: invitation card</p><p class="gloss">抽屜: drawer</p><p class="gloss">集合處: meeting point</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. How does Anhe’s understanding change after the conversation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從不想參加，變爲被要求立刻送出禮物</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 從已經收到卡片，變爲認定照片中的活動是假的</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 從認爲被排斥，變爲知道邀請卡放錯了班級</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which conclusion is best supported by her final actions?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 她願意表達感受，也通過覈對具體信息繼續參與</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 她認定每次沒收到邀請都一定只是教室號碼錯了</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她決定以後只要有照片就不必問時間地點</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">綠地提示牌提案：用美術室剩下的硬紙板做牌，寫清可以走的小路和不能進入的新種苗區。學校提供可重複使用的夾子和支架，牌子夾在支架上，不往樹上釘，也不爲每個經過的人另印一張。每組先畫草稿，請老師看清楚後再寫正式牌。<br>補充通知：週六上午有雨，大家十點先到美術室做牌，不到綠地放置。等天晴且老師在場時，再一起討論放在哪裏。小余只有週六上午能來，希望自己的部分那天做完。她可以先負責畫清楚一塊牌的路線，覈對後把成品牌留在美術室，另請以後有空的組員隨老師放置，而不是自己下雨時搶先把牌釘到樹上。</p></div><p class="gloss">硬紙板: cardboard</p><p class="gloss">支架: stand</p><p class="gloss">放置: put in position</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the school provide for displaying the signs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每位路人一份新印的紙本</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 可重複使用的夾子和支架</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把牌釘到樹上所需的工具</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan fits Xiaoyu’s availability and both notices?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 爲週六做完全部步驟，下雨時自己把牌釘到樹上</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週六室內核稿做牌，留給有空組員隨老師擇晴天放置</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 直接跳過草稿和核對，讓路人各領一張新紙</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">本週綠地觀察活動試行少印紙：路線說明放在集合處的大字公共板上，不給每個人自動發一份。需要近處閱讀，或要帶回家覈對時間的同學，仍可領取紙本。這個辦法只先用於本次活動，不等於以後所有通知都改成電子版。結束後，負責人會收集大家的使用意見，再決定下一次怎樣做。</p></div><p class="gloss">試行: trial implementation</p><p class="gloss">紙本: paper copy</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which description matches the reduced-printing trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 本次用公共板爲主，有需要的人仍可領紙本</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 從此所有通知只能在網上看，完全不發紙本</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 無論參加者是否需要，每人自動發三份路線表</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安的記錄：剛參加攝影社時，我每個週六跟着大家連跑幾個地方，想多拍一些照片，回家後卻沒時間整理，也覺得很趕。最近兩週，我改成上午只在一個地方觀察四十五分鐘，拍完先選幾張、寫下注意到什麼。這兩個週六的下午，我都沒有再趕去下一個地點，而是留在家裏休息或做別的事。<br>同伴回覆：你還想觀察有意思的細節，也想讓週末有空餘，可以再試幾次這個安排。照片少了，不等於沒有學習。小安補充：我想下週看看遇到社團特別活動時怎樣調整。現在只記錄了兩個週六，不能說所有人少去幾個地方都會有一樣的感受，也不能認定以後永遠不換地點。</p></div><p class="gloss">攝影社: photography club</p><p class="gloss">空餘: free time</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoan explicitly report over the two Saturdays?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 已經決定以後永遠不再更換拍攝地點</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上午不再拍照，也不整理任何照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 下午沒有再趕去下一個拍攝地點</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does the reply suggest trying this arrangement a few more times?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲兩週已證明只拍四十五分鐘適合所有人</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因爲照片一少，攝影社就不再要求任何學習</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 它保留觀察細節的興趣，也回應週末想有空餘的需要</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">剛到新班時，我參加了一次校園介紹活動，提前把許多地名背了下來，怕別人問什麼我都不會。真正開始以後，我很少用到那些長說明。帶隊的同學反而請我說一個自己想了解的問題，大家一起去找答案。我問了圖書角什麼時候能借書，後來另一位新同學說，她也一直想問。<br>現在我準備參加新的社團介紹，每週只有兩次午休能做準備。我決定先寫兩個真實的問題，再看相關通知，不把每個角落的名稱都背一遍。遇到還不能確定的內容，就標出來當場詢問。上次我以爲準備得越多、說得越長越好，這次出門前檢查的是：問題是否清楚，哪些已有答案，哪些還要一起找。</p></div><p class="gloss">帶隊: lead a group</p><p class="gloss">當場: on the spot</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which preparation fits both the earlier experience and the present time limit?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 繼續背所有長說明，直到每個地名都完全記熟</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不準備任何問題，認定別人一定會替自己問完</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先準備兩個真實問題，查相關通知並標出待詢問處</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What changed view is supported by the final checklist?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 準備可以更有針對性，保留尚需一起找答案的問題</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要問題真實，就完全不必查任何現有通知</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 在新班級裏，只有背出最多地名的人才算參與</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to an earlier media-project deadline</h2><p>Reply to Zhou in Chinese. Say whether you can join Tuesday’s lunchtime topic meeting. Choose a campus-corner introduction, a new-student question-and-answer programme or another relevant topic and explain why. State a part you can prepare. Give a feasible plan for the earlier Thursday deadline, and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安：我們要做校園廣播項目，你週二午休能來選題嗎？你更想介紹校園角落，還是做新同學問答？你能準備哪部分？原來週五晚上交，現在改爲週四下午六點前，錄音和文字稿都要一起交。請提個能按時完成的辦法，也問清你還需要知道的事。<br>小舟</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can attend Tuesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose a relevant topic and explain a reason.</li><li>State a part you can prepare.</li><li>Propose preparation and submission that fit the earlier Thursday deadline.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>A learning experience that changed an expectation</h2><p>Use the fictional activity card to write connected Chinese paragraphs about a learning experience that changed your view. Include time and context, at least two actions in sequence, expectation versus outcome, a reason or feeling, and one reflection or next step. Add plausible details consistent with the card if useful. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虛構學習卡<br>時間：上個月一個週日下午<br>地點與活動：活動中心，第一次學摺紙<br>原先期待：看圖很簡單，幾分鐘完成，還想帶一個給朋友<br>經過：只看最後的樣子，兩次沒做好；展開紙；與同伴逐步看圖，發現第二步方向反了；重做<br>結果：花時比預計長，但做出能立起來的紙房子，也能說明改了哪裏<br>感受與下一步：自行選擇，須與事實一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Sunday afternoon and a first paper-folding session.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with the actual outcome.</li><li>Explain a feeling or a reason.</li><li>Give a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Choose and adapt learning-support materials</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate planning a Chinese-learning support activity. Each file already includes two plays; play the file once, then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Explain a preference using an experience, adapt to a new resource limit and agree on a next step. Personal details may be invented. All four turns together form one task /8, not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate will run a short Chinese-learning support activity. A change of resources is introduced in the third prompt.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State a preference or learning need with a reason.</li><li>Link a past experience to that preference.</li><li>Adapt materials to no internet while a computer remains available.</li><li>Give a final arrangement, own preparation and a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Compare two learning-support plans</h2><p>Recommend one of the two learning-support plans to your class. Compare a relevant feature of both, use two different details from the card to support your choice, acknowledge a limitation and propose a practical next step. Either plan can receive full credit if its constraints and actual participation are addressed. Prepare for 60 seconds and speak for up to 120 seconds. Use the on-screen card; there is no separate audio question.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班級情況：18人，週二、三、四午休都有空；其中13人週六上午有空。希望儘量讓更多人獲得支持，也重視提問機會；總材料預算50元。<br>甲：週二、三、四午休各一場，12:40–13:00，每場最多6人，每人本週只報一場；免費；週一17:00前按場次登記並交問題。三場各有6個位置，按確認名單參加。<br>乙：週六9:00–10:30集中學習，最多18人；全組材料費40元；週四18:00前報名，須帶自己的問題卡。不能參加者可領取已有資料，但不算參加現場討論。<br>可以推薦任一方案，須說明實際參與範圍、時間、準備與限制。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Use one supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Use a different supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Acknowledge a limitation of the recommended plan.</li><li>Give a feasible next step addressing the limitation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>